---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Working Principle of Four-Stroke Petrol Engine - Complete 720° Cycle"
  description="Learn the complete mechanical and thermodynamic working principle of a 4-stroke spark ignition petrol engine: Intake, Compression, Power, and Exhaust strokes."
>
  <div class="container page-header">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <span>Working Principle</span>
    </div>
    <h1 style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Working Principle of a Four-Stroke Petrol Engine</h1>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 720px; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
      Detailed step-by-step examination of the four strokes constituting a complete 720° engine cycle.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="container" style="padding-bottom: 3.5rem;">
    <div class="strokes-timeline">
      <!-- Stroke 1 -->
      <article class="eng-card stroke-timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-header">
          <span class="badge badge-intake">Stroke 1: 0° to 180° Crankshaft Angle</span>
          <h2>Intake (Suction) Stroke</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-spec">
            <p><strong>Piston Travel:</strong> Top Dead Centre (TDC) to Bottom Dead Centre (BDC)</p>
            <p><strong>Inlet Valve:</strong> OPEN (lift up to 8.5 mm)</p>
            <p><strong>Exhaust Valve:</strong> CLOSED</p>
            <p><strong>Cylinder Pressure:</strong> ~0.90 to 0.98 bar (slight depression below atmospheric)</p>
          </div>
          <p class="timeline-narrative">
            As the crankshaft rotates from 0° to 180°, the connecting rod draws the piston downward. The increasing cylinder volume creates a partial vacuum (depression) inside the cylinder. The pressure difference between the intake manifold (atmospheric pressure) and the inside of the cylinder forces fresh atmospheric air mixed with atomized fuel (or direct-injected fuel) through the open inlet valve port into the cylinder.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Stroke 2 -->
      <article class="eng-card stroke-timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-header">
          <span class="badge badge-compression">Stroke 2: 180° to 360° Crankshaft Angle</span>
          <h2>Compression Stroke</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-spec">
            <p><strong>Piston Travel:</strong> Bottom Dead Centre (BDC) to Top Dead Centre (TDC)</p>
            <p><strong>Inlet Valve:</strong> CLOSED</p>
            <p><strong>Exhaust Valve:</strong> CLOSED</p>
            <p><strong>Cylinder Pressure:</strong> Rises from 1 bar up to ~15–20 bar at TDC</p>
          </div>
          <p class="timeline-narrative">
            Both valves remain hermetically sealed. As the crankshaft continues rotating through its second half-revolution (180° to 360°), the piston moves upward towards the cylinder head, squeezing the trapped combustible charge into the small clearance volume (Vc). According to polytropic compression (P · V^1.34 = constant), gas pressure rises to 15–20 bar and temperature rises to 350–450 °C. Near 15°–20° BTDC, the spark plug initiates an electrical discharge arc.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Stroke 3 -->
      <article class="eng-card stroke-timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-header">
          <span class="badge badge-power">Stroke 3: 360° to 540° Crankshaft Angle</span>
          <h2>Power (Expansion) Stroke</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-spec">
            <p><strong>Piston Travel:</strong> Top Dead Centre (TDC) to Bottom Dead Centre (BDC)</p>
            <p><strong>Inlet Valve:</strong> CLOSED</p>
            <p><strong>Exhaust Valve:</strong> CLOSED (opens near 490°–500° before BDC)</p>
            <p><strong>Cylinder Pressure:</strong> Peaks at ~45–60 bar, then expands to ~3.5 bar</p>
          </div>
          <p class="timeline-narrative">
            The spark ignites the compressed mixture. Rapid chemical deflagration releases immense thermal energy, raising gas temperature to 2,000–2,500 K and pressure to 45–60 bar. These high-pressure gases exert a tremendous downward force on the piston crown ($F = P \times A$). The piston is thrust downward from TDC to BDC, transmitting mechanical torque to the crankshaft via the connecting rod. This is the sole stroke that delivers positive mechanical work to the system.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Stroke 4 -->
      <article class="eng-card stroke-timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-header">
          <span class="badge badge-exhaust">Stroke 4: 540° to 720° Crankshaft Angle</span>
          <h2>Exhaust Stroke</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-spec">
            <p><strong>Piston Travel:</strong> Bottom Dead Centre (BDC) to Top Dead Centre (TDC)</p>
            <p><strong>Inlet Valve:</strong> CLOSED (opens slightly before TDC in realistic timing)</p>
            <p><strong>Exhaust Valve:</strong> OPEN</p>
            <p><strong>Cylinder Pressure:</strong> ~1.05 to 1.15 bar (slight exhaust backpressure)</p>
          </div>
          <p class="timeline-narrative">
            The exhaust valve opens. Momentum stored in the heavy rotating flywheel drives the crankshaft through its final half-revolution, propelling the piston upward from BDC to TDC. The ascending piston mechanically pushes out the burnt exhaust gases through the open exhaust port into the exhaust manifold. At 720° (TDC), the engine seamlessly transitions into the next intake stroke, continuing the cyclic operation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }
  .strokes-timeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .stroke-timeline-item {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .timeline-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .timeline-content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.6fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .timeline-spec {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .timeline-spec strong {
    color: var(--text-main);
  }
  .timeline-narrative {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .timeline-content {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>

